@startuml acknowledge-flow
title US-13: Acknowledge Flow - Durable Transition + Distributed Lifecycle Fan-Out

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as TSDB
database "Redis\nalert-events" as AlertEvents
participant "API\n(all instances)" as APIAll

Operator -> Dashboard : click Acknowledge
Dashboard -> API : PATCH /alerts/{alert_id}\n{ status: ACKNOWLEDGED }

API -> TSDB : UPDATE alerts\nSET status='ACKNOWLEDGED', acknowledged_at=..., acknowledged_by=...\nWHERE alert_id=$id AND status='NEW'
TSDB --> API : transitioned row or no-op

alt row transitioned NEW -> ACKNOWLEDGED
  API -> AlertEvents : PUBLISH ALERT_STATUS_CHANGED\n{ alert_id, status: ACKNOWLEDGED, ... }
  AlertEvents --> APIAll : lifecycle event
  APIAll --> Dashboard : WebSocket lifecycle update
else already ACKNOWLEDGED / terminal / invalid transition
  API --> Dashboard : return current durable state\n(no duplicate transition event required)
end

note over TSDB
  Durable DB state is authoritative.
  ACKNOWLEDGED remains active and may later be
  superseded by a COMPOSITE system transition.
  RESOLVED and SUPERSEDED are terminal.
end note

note over AlertEvents, Dashboard
  WebSocket lifecycle delivery is at-least-once.
  Clients converge by alert_id + durable lifecycle state.
end note

@enduml
